* =====================================================================================================
* led_data__sn74lv1t34.lib -- SN74LV1T34 single buffer with reduced (TTL-like) input thresholds
*                             (DNP LED-data level shifter U43, VCC = VLED, A = LED_DIN_R, Y = LED_DIN)
*
* Part      : Texas Instruments SN74LV1T34DBVR (SOT-23-5: 1 NC, 2 A, 3 GND, 4 Y, 5 VCC), LCSC C100024.
* Datasheet : SN74LV1T34, SCLS743E (December 2013, revised February 2024),
*             https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74lv1t34.pdf
*             6.1 Absolute maximum ratings: VCC/VI -0.5 ... 7.0 V, VO -0.5 ... VCC + 0.5 V, IO +/-25 mA.
*             6.3 Recommended operating conditions: VCC 1.6-5.5 V, VI 0-5.5 V, IOH -7 mA (3.3 V) / -8 mA
*                 (5.0 V), dt/dv <= 20 ns/V (VCC 3.3 V and 5.0 V).
*             6.5 Electrical characteristics (TA = -40 ... 125 C column used for worst case):
*                 VIH min: 1.39 V (VCC 3.0-3.3 V), 1.48 V (3.6 V), 2.03 V (4.5-5.0 V), 2.11 V (5.5 V)
*                 VIL max: 0.65 V (VCC 3.0-3.6 V), 0.8 V (4.5-5.5 V)
*                 VOH: VCC 3.0 V: 2.7 V @ -3 mA, 2.49 V @ -5.5 mA; 3.3 V: 2.8 V @ -5.5 mA;
*                      4.5 V: 4.1 V @ -4 mA, 3.95 V @ -8 mA; 5.0 V: 4.5 V @ -8 mA
*                      -> worst chord pull-up resistance (VCC - VOH)/|IOH| = 100 ohm (RUP default)
*                 VOL: 3.0 V: 0.15 V @ 3 mA, 0.252 V @ 5.5 mA; 4.5 V: 0.2 V @ 4 mA, 0.35 V @ 8 mA
*                      -> worst chord pull-down resistance 50 ohm (RDN default)
*                 Ci (A) typ 2 pF / max 10 pF (CI default 10 pF); Co typ 2.5 pF.
*             6.6 Switching characteristics, tpd A->Y, CL = 15 pF, TA -65 ... 125 C max:
*                 5.0 V 6.5 ns, 3.3 V 8 ns, 2.5 V 9.5 ns (typ 25 C: 2.7 / 4.0 / 5.8 ns).
*
* Modelled  : input capacitance; a switching threshold VTH (parameter, set by the test anywhere between
*             the VIL max and VIH min of the actual VCC to bracket the real threshold); separate internal
*             delays for the rising (TDR) and the falling (TDF) output edge (XSPICE adc_bridge -> d_buffer
*             -> dac_bridge, event driven; needs ngspice with XSPICE code models, standard in ngspice 42),
*             so a tPLH/tPHL skew corner can be applied; a rail-to-rail CMOS output stage made of chord
*             resistances RUP/RDN switched by a first-order pre-driver with 10-90 % edge TEDGE, plus Co.
*             The test sets TDR/TDF = tpd(VCC) - (simulated output-stage delay into 15 pF), so the model tpd
*             into 15 pF equals the 6.6 maximum, and re-checks that against the table (0.95 ... 1.01 x).
*             The input threshold is referenced to the global ground node (gnd must be node 0).
*             TEDGE (output pre-driver 10-90 %) is NOT in the DS: 1 ns is an assumption; it is absorbed by
*             the tpd calibration and only shapes the edge.
*
* NOT modelled: the input structure's extra supply current when VI < VCC (6.5 delta-ICC); Ioff/power-down
*             behaviour; output current limiting beyond the chord resistance; ESD clamps on A
*             (A tolerates 7 V abs max independent of VCC); the tpd minimum (not given in the DS: the skew
*             corner uses 0 ... tpd max); any metastability or input hysteresis (none specified).
*
* Pins: a, y, vcc, gnd
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt SN74LV1T34 a y vcc gnd params: VTH=1.5 TDR=5n TDF=5n RUP=100 RDN=50 TEDGE=1n CI=10p CO=2.5p
Ci a gnd {CI}
* input threshold + separate tPLH / tPHL as XSPICE digital primitives (robust event-driven delays)
Aadc [a] [da] lv_adc
.model lv_adc adc_bridge(in_low={VTH} in_high={VTH} rise_delay=1e-12 fall_delay=1e-12)
Abuf da db lv_buf
.model lv_buf d_buffer(rise_delay={max(TDR,1e-12)} fall_delay={max(TDF,1e-12)} input_load=0)
Adac [db] [x] lv_dac
.model lv_dac dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 out_undef=0.5 t_rise=1e-11 t_fall=1e-11)
* pre-driver and output stage
Rpre x s 1k
Cpre s gnd {TEDGE/2.1972/1k}
Bup vcc y I = max(min(v(s,gnd),1),0)*v(vcc,y)/RUP
Bdn y gnd I = max(min(1-v(s,gnd),1),0)*v(y,gnd)/RDN
Co y gnd {CO}
.ends SN74LV1T34
